# ====================================================================
# Vivado Project Gitignore (Optimized for Pure Verilog/VHDL Projects)
# Keeps ONLY core project structure (.xpr), code (.v, .sv, .xdc), and Block Designs (.bd)
# ====================================================================

# --- Vivado Logs, Journals and Temporary Files ---
*.log
*.jou
*.str
*.os
*.vdi
*.pp
.Xil/

# --- Simulation & Testbench Artifacts ---
xsim.dir/
*.pb
*.wdb
*.vcd
*.exe

# --- Compilation, Bitstream & Debug Outputs ---
*.bit
*.bin
*.ltx
*.mcs
*.prm
*.sys
*.mem

# --- Lab Tools & Hardware Manager Data (.hw folder) ---
*.lpr
.hw/

# --- Vivado Cache & WebTalk Telemetry (.cache/wt) ---
.cache/
**/wt/

# --- Local Workspace User Settings & Autogenerated Directories ---
# Vivado will automatically recreate these when you open the .xpr
.srcs/
.gen/
.sim/
.ip_user_files/
.runs/
.data/

# --- Block Designs (If used, ignores autogenerated wrappers but keeps core structure) ---
**/*.bd.tcl
**/bd/*/hdl/
**/bd/*/ip/
**/bd/*/hw_handoff/
**/bd/*/ui/
**/bd/*/ipshared/

# --- System & OS Files ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db